State:
	ts[t] = best choice of task at time t
Choices:
	task at time t
Transition/recurrence:
	for each task:
		- is it available/able to be executed late?
		- recurse on choice of task
Base case:
	- No more tasks available to be chosen: All tasks are either
		- already chosen
		- past deadline (no dependencies)
		- all dependencies all past deadline
			- recursive chain to examine dependency list?
Evaluation order:
	Memoization vs tabulation
	- Memoization:
		- Pros:
			- mirrors mathematical recurrence
			- computes only reachable states
		- Costs:
			- hash/array lookup + recursion stack
			- may hit recursion-depth limits
	- Tabulation:
		- Pros:
			- no recursion overhead
			- memory layout preditable + cache-friendly
		- Costs:
			- may compute extra states

	Decision: Memoization
	- easy to implement recursive function directly from logic
	- reconstructing solution can be done by referencing earlier method from past homework

